  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Writing strategy$q$, 'mc', $q$A paragraph describes how a librarian started a seed library where people borrow seeds and return seeds from their harvest. The writer considers ending with: "Seeds are small."$q$, $q$Should the writer add this sentence?$q$, $q$["Yes, because it summarizes the paragraph.", "No, because it contradicts the paragraph.", "Yes, because it describes the seeds.", "No, because it adds nothing meaningful about the seed library."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The sentence is trivial and doesn't develop the paragraph's idea.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Writing strategy$q$, 'mc', $q$Passage: "Before the race, Tara stretched for ten minutes. [[She had trained for months.]] Then she took her place at the starting line."$q$, $q$The writer wants this sentence to explain why Tara felt confident. Which choice best accomplishes this?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "The weather was cloudy.", "Months of training had prepared her for this moment, and she knew it.", "Her shoes were new."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Only this choice links her training to her confidence.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Writing strategy$q$, 'mc', $q$An essay argues that schools should start later in the morning. The writer wants to add evidence. Which choice is the most relevant?$q$, $q$Which choice best accomplishes the writer's goal?$q$, $q$["Some students walk to school.", "Studies of schools that moved start times later found students slept more and were tardy less often.", "School buses are usually yellow.", "Many schools have a cafeteria."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Only this choice is evidence about later start times.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Writing strategy$q$, 'mc', $q$Sentence 1: Next, she sanded the tabletop until it was smooth. Sentence 2: First, Lena removed the old paint with a scraper. Sentence 3: Finally, she applied two coats of varnish.$q$, $q$Which order makes the paragraph most logical?$q$, $q$["2, 1, 3", "1, 3, 2", "3, 2, 1", "1, 2, 3"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The words First, Next and Finally give the order: 2, 1, 3.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Concision$q$, 'mc', $q$The meeting was postponed [[until a later time in the future]].$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "to a later future date", "until a future time later on", "until later"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$"Postponed until later" says it all; "in the future" repeats "later."$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Concision$q$, 'mc', $q$She [[made a decision to]] join the debate team.$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "made the decision of deciding to", "decided to", "had a decision made to"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$"Decided" is shorter and clearer.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Concision$q$, 'mc', $q$The [[final end result]] of the experiment surprised everyone.$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "resulting end", "result", "end final result"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$"Final" and "end" repeat each other; "result" alone is enough.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Concision$q$, 'mc', $q$Each and every student [[must be required to]] bring a calculator.$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "must be needed to be required to", "is required and must", "must"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$"Must" already means required.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Concision$q$, 'mc', $q$The two friends met together [[at the same time]] every Friday.$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "at the same time together", "simultaneously at once", "DELETE the underlined portion and end the sentence with \"every Friday.\""]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Meeting together already happens at the same time; delete the redundant phrase.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Concision$q$, 'mc', $q$[[In my personal opinion, I think]] the movie was too long.$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "Personally, in my opinion,", "In my opinion, I personally think", "I think"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$"In my personal opinion" and "I think" say the same thing.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Word choice$q$, 'mc', $q$The scientist's findings were [[real good]].$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "really good-like", "good real", "impressive"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$"Real good" is too casual for a formal essay; "impressive" is precise.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Word choice$q$, 'mc', $q$The ancient city was [[discovered]] in 1911 by explorers searching the mountains.$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "invented", "made up", "come across"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Explorers find places; they don't invent them. The original is correct.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Word choice$q$, 'mc', $q$The senator gave a [[super awesome]] speech about clean water.$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "powerful", "totally sweet", "kind of okay"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The essay is formal, so "powerful" fits the tone better than slang.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Word choice$q$, 'mc', $q$The heavy rain [[caused]] the river to overflow its banks.$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "persuaded", "convinced", "let"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Rain causes a flood; it doesn't persuade a river. The original is correct.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Word choice$q$, 'mc', $q$The museum's collection is [[comprised of]] over 3,000 works of art.$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "made up of", "composed by", "comprising of"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$"Made up of" is clear and correct. "Comprised of" is widely considered nonstandard in formal writing.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Word choice$q$, 'mc', $q$The hikers were [[anxious]] to reach the summit and see the view.$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "worried", "eager", "nervous"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$They are looking forward to the view, so "eager" fits. "Anxious" suggests worry.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Tone$q$, 'mc', $q$In a formal letter to a city council, a student writes: "[[You guys need to]] fix the potholes on Main Street."$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "I respectfully ask the council to", "Come on and", "Y'all should"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$A formal letter calls for a respectful tone.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT English$q$, $q$Tone$q$, 'mc', $q$The essay describes a solemn memorial ceremony. "The crowd stood quietly as the names were [[yelled out]]."$q$, $q$Which choice is best?$q$, $q$["NO CHANGE", "hollered", "read aloud", "blurted"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$"Read aloud" matches the solemn mood.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Percentages$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is 15% of 240?$q$, $q$["16", "24", "36", "160"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$0.15 × 240 = 36. (10% is 24 and 5% is 12; 24 + 12 = 36.)$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Linear equations$q$, 'mc', null, $q$If 5x + 3 = 2x − 12, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["−5", "−3", "3", "5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Subtract 2x: 3x + 3 = −12. Subtract 3: 3x = −15, so x = −5.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Lines$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the slope of the line 6x − 2y = 8?$q$, $q$["−4", "−3", "3", "6"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Solve for y: −2y = −6x + 8, so y = 3x − 4. The slope is 3.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Ratios$q$, 'mc', null, $q$The ratio of boys to girls in a club is 3:5. If the club has 40 members, how many are girls?$q$, $q$["8", "15", "24", "25"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$3 + 5 = 8 parts, so each part is 40 / 8 = 5 members. Girls: 5 × 5 = 25.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Number sense$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the value of |−7| − |3 − 10|?$q$, $q$["−14", "0", "4", "14"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$|−7| = 7 and |3 − 10| = |−7| = 7, so 7 − 7 = 0.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Exponents$q$, 'mc', null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (2x²y)³?$q$, $q$["8x⁶y³", "2x⁶y³", "8x⁵y³", "6x⁶y³"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Cube each factor: 2³ = 8, (x²)³ = x⁶, y³. Multiply the exponents when raising a power to a power.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Area$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the area of a triangle with a base of 14 and a height of 9?$q$, $q$["23", "31.5", "63", "126"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Area = ½ × base × height = ½ × 14 × 9 = 63.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Coordinate geometry$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the midpoint of the segment with endpoints (−2, 5) and (6, −1)?$q$, $q$["(2, 2)", "(2, 3)", "(4, −3)", "(4, 4)"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Average the coordinates: ((−2 + 6) / 2, (5 + (−1)) / 2) = (2, 2).$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Coordinate geometry$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the distance between the points (1, 2) and (4, 6)?$q$, $q$["√7", "5", "7", "25"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The differences are 3 and 4, and √(3² + 4²) = √25 = 5.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Logarithms$q$, 'mc', null, $q$If log₂(x) = 5, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["7", "10", "25", "32"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$log₂(x) = 5 means 2⁵ = x, so x = 32.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Quadratics$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the sum of the solutions of x² − 9x + 20 = 0?$q$, $q$["−9", "4", "9", "20"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Factor: (x − 4)(x − 5) = 0, so x = 4 or 5, and 4 + 5 = 9.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Trigonometry$q$, 'mc', null, $q$In right triangle ABC, angle C is 90°, AC = 8 and BC = 6. What is tan A?$q$, $q$["3/4", "4/3", "4/5", "3/5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$tan A = opposite / adjacent. The side opposite A is BC = 6 and the side next to A is AC = 8, so 6/8 = 3/4.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Sequences$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the next term in the sequence 3, 6, 12, 24, ...?$q$, $q$["27", "30", "36", "48"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Each term is double the one before, so 24 × 2 = 48.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Functions$q$, 'mc', null, $q$If f(x) = 3x − 1 and g(x) = x², what is f(g(2))?$q$, $q$["5", "11", "12", "25"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Work inside out: g(2) = 4, then f(4) = 3(4) − 1 = 11. (25 is g(f(2)).)$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Percentages$q$, 'mc', null, $q$The price of a shirt went from $40 to $50. By what percent did the price increase?$q$, $q$["10%", "20%", "25%", "50%"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Percent change = change / original = 10 / 40 = 25%. Divide by the original price, not the new one.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Number sense$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the least common multiple of 6, 8 and 12?$q$, $q$["12", "24", "48", "96"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$24 is the smallest number that 6, 8 and 12 all divide into evenly.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Inequalities$q$, 'mc', null, $q$Which describes all solutions of 2(x − 3) ≥ 10?$q$, $q$["x ≤ 8", "x ≥ 8", "x ≥ 6.5", "x ≥ 2"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Divide by 2: x − 3 ≥ 5. Add 3: x ≥ 8. (The sign only flips when you multiply or divide by a negative.)$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Complex numbers$q$, 'mc', null, $q$If i = √−1, what is the value of i² + i⁴?$q$, $q$["−2", "0", "2i", "2"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$i² = −1 and i⁴ = (i²)² = 1, so the sum is 0.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 'mc', null, $q$A circle has a circumference of 12π. What is its area?$q$, $q$["12π", "144π", "36π", "6π"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$C = 2πr = 12π, so r = 6. Area = πr² = 36π.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Counting$q$, 'mc', null, $q$How many different 3-letter codes can be made from the letters A, B, C, D and E if no letter may repeat?$q$, $q$["10", "15", "60", "125"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$5 choices for the first letter, 4 for the second and 3 for the third: 5 × 4 × 3 = 60.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Trigonometry$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the period of the function y = sin(2x)?$q$, $q$["π/2", "π", "4π", "2π"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The period of sin(bx) is 2π / b = 2π / 2 = π.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Statistics$q$, 'mc', null, $q$The average of x, 2x and 3x is 18. What is the value of x?$q$, $q$["3", "6", "9", "18"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$(x + 2x + 3x) / 3 = 2x = 18, so x = 9.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Number sense$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the greatest common factor of 36 and 60?$q$, $q$["4", "6", "12", "180"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$36 = 2² · 3² and 60 = 2² · 3 · 5. Shared: 2² · 3 = 12.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Number sense$q$, 'mc', null, $q$Which of the following is a prime number?$q$, $q$["27", "29", "33", "39"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$29 has no factors other than 1 and itself. 27 = 3 · 9, 33 = 3 · 11, 39 = 3 · 13.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Number sense$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the value of 3 − (−5) + (−2)?$q$, $q$["−4", "0", "6", "10"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$3 + 5 − 2 = 6. Subtracting a negative is adding.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Number sense$q$, 'mc', null, $q$Which value is greatest?$q$, $q$["0.6", "0.58", "5/9", "4/7"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$5/9 ≈ 0.556 and 4/7 ≈ 0.571, so 0.6 is greatest.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Number sense$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is 2.4 × 10⁻³ written in standard form?$q$, $q$["0.00024", "0.0024", "0.024", "2,400"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Move the decimal 3 places left: 0.0024.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Radicals$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is √50 in simplest radical form?$q$, $q$["5√2", "2√5", "25√2", "10√5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$√50 = √(25 · 2) = 5√2.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Radicals$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the value of √18 + √8?$q$, $q$["5√2", "13√2", "√26", "2√13"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$√18 = 3√2 and √8 = 2√2, so the sum is 5√2.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Complex numbers$q$, 'mc', null, $q$If i = √−1, what is (3 + 2i)(3 − 2i)?$q$, $q$["5", "9 − 4i", "13", "9 + 4i"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$(3)² − (2i)² = 9 − 4i² = 9 + 4 = 13.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Matrices$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the sum of the matrices [2 5] and [−1 4]?$q$, $q$["[1 9]", "[−2 20]", "[3 1]", "[1 1]"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Add matching entries: 2 + (−1) = 1 and 5 + 4 = 9.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Number sense$q$, 'mc', null, $q$A number is divisible by both 4 and 6. Which of the following must also divide it?$q$, $q$["8", "10", "12", "24"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The least common multiple of 4 and 6 is 12, so the number is a multiple of 12. It need not be a multiple of 24 (12 itself works).$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Linear equations$q$, 'mc', null, $q$If 3(x − 4) = 2x + 1, what is x?$q$, $q$["−11", "5", "11", "13"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$3x − 12 = 2x + 1, so x = 13.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Linear equations$q$, 'mc', null, $q$Solve for w: P = 2l + 2w.$q$, $q$["w = 2P − 2l", "w = P − l", "w = (P + 2l) / 2", "w = (P − 2l) / 2"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Subtract 2l: P − 2l = 2w. Divide by 2.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Linear equations$q$, 'mc', null, $q$If x/4 + x/2 = 9, what is x?$q$, $q$["6", "12", "18", "36"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Multiply by 4: x + 2x = 36, so 3x = 36 and x = 12.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Systems of equations$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the solution (x, y) of the system x + y = 9 and 2x − y = 6?$q$, $q$["(5, 4)", "(4, 5)", "(6, 3)", "(3, 6)"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Add: 3x = 15, so x = 5 and y = 4.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Quadratics$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What are the solutions of x² − 6x + 8 = 0?$q$, $q$["1 and 8", "2 and 4", "−2 and 4", "−2 and −4"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Factor: (x − 2)(x − 4) = 0.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Quadratics$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What are the solutions of x² = 5x?$q$, $q$["5 only", "0 only", "0 and 5", "−5 and 5"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$x² − 5x = 0 → x(x − 5) = 0. Don't divide by x, or you lose x = 0.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Quadratics$q$, 'mc', null, $q$Using the quadratic formula, what are the solutions of x² + 2x − 1 = 0?$q$, $q$["−1 ± 2√2", "1 ± √2", "−1 ± √2", "−2 ± √2"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$x = [−2 ± √(4 + 4)] / 2 = (−2 ± 2√2) / 2 = −1 ± √2.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Polynomials$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is (2x² + 3x − 5) − (x² − 4x + 2)?$q$, $q$["x² + 7x − 3", "3x² − x − 3", "x² − x − 3", "x² + 7x − 7"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Subtract each term: 2x² − x² = x², 3x − (−4x) = 7x, −5 − 2 = −7.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Polynomials$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the product (x + 3)(x² − 2)?$q$, $q$["x³ + 3x² + 2x − 6", "x³ + 3x² − 6", "x³ + 3x² − 2x − 6", "x³ − 2x + 3"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$x · x² = x³, x · (−2) = −2x, 3 · x² = 3x², 3 · (−2) = −6.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Inequalities$q$, 'mc', null, $q$Which describes all solutions of |x − 3| < 5?$q$, $q$["x < 8", "−8 < x < 2", "x < −2 or x > 8", "−2 < x < 8"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$|x − 3| < 5 means −5 < x − 3 < 5, so −2 < x < 8.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Inequalities$q$, 'mc', null, $q$Which number line description matches x ≤ −1 or x > 4?$q$, $q$["Shaded between −1 and 4", "Shaded right from −1 only", "Shaded left from a closed dot at −1, and right from an open dot at 4", "Shaded left from an open dot at −1, and right from a closed dot at 4"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$≤ uses a closed dot; > uses an open dot. "Or" shades two separate pieces.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Exponents$q$, 'mc', null, $q$If 2^x = 32 and 3^y = 9, what is x + y?$q$, $q$["5", "6", "7", "41"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$2⁵ = 32 so x = 5, and 3² = 9 so y = 2. 5 + 2 = 7.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Exponents$q$, 'mc', null, $q$Which expression is equivalent to (a³b²)(a²b⁴)?$q$, $q$["a⁶b⁸", "a⁵b⁶", "a⁶b⁶", "a⁵b⁸"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Add exponents on matching bases: a³⁺² = a⁵, b²⁺⁴ = b⁶.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Rational expressions$q$, 'mc', null, $q$For x ≠ 0, which expression is equivalent to (x² − 3x) / x?$q$, $q$["x² − 3", "x − 3", "x + 3", "−3x"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Factor x out of the top: x(x − 3) / x = x − 3.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Functions$q$, 'mc', null, $q$If f(x) = x² − 2x, what is f(−3)?$q$, $q$["−15", "−3", "3", "15"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$(−3)² − 2(−3) = 9 + 6 = 15.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Functions$q$, 'mc', null, $q$If f(x) = 4x − 7, what value of x makes f(x) = 9?$q$, $q$["0.5", "2", "4", "29"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$4x − 7 = 9, so 4x = 16 and x = 4.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Functions$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the domain of f(x) = √(x − 6)?$q$, $q$["All real numbers", "x ≥ 0", "x > 6", "x ≥ 6"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The expression under a square root must be at least 0: x − 6 ≥ 0.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Functions$q$, 'mc', null, $q$What is the range of f(x) = x² + 3?$q$, $q$["y ≤ 3", "All real numbers", "y ≥ 0", "y ≥ 3"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$x² is never negative, so x² + 3 is at least 3.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Functions$q$, 'mc', null, $q$If f(x) = 2x and g(x) = x + 5, what is g(f(3))?$q$, $q$["10", "11", "13", "16"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$f(3) = 6, then g(6) = 11.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Functions$q$, 'mc', null, $q$Which function is the graph of y = x² shifted 4 units to the right?$q$, $q$["y = (x + 4)²", "y = (x − 4)²", "y = x² − 4", "y = x² + 4"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Replacing x with (x − 4) shifts a graph right 4 units.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Functions$q$, 'mc', null, $q$The inverse of f(x) = 3x + 6 is:$q$, $q$["f⁻¹(x) = (x − 6) / 3", "f⁻¹(x) = 1 / (3x + 6)", "f⁻¹(x) = (x + 6) / 3", "f⁻¹(x) = 3x − 6"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Swap x and y: x = 3y + 6, so y = (x − 6) / 3.$q$),
  ('ACT', $q$ACT Math$q$, $q$Functions$q$, 'mc', null, $q$Which describes the end behavior of f(x) = −2x³?$q$, $q$["f(x) approaches 0 as x increases.", "As x increases, f(x) increases without bound.", "As x increases, f(x) decreases without bound.", "f(x) approaches −2 as x increases."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$A cubic with a negative leading coefficient goes down to the right.$q$),
