Scientists are still working to understand how monarchs find the same small patches of forest year after year. Some suspect that the butterflies also sense Earth's magnetic field, especially on cloudy days when the sun is hidden.$q$, $q$In the antenna study, the group with clear paint was most likely included to:$q$, $q$["make the butterflies easier to see", "test whether butterflies prefer clear skies", "measure how far butterflies can fly", "show that the paint itself was not what disrupted navigation"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The clear-paint group got paint but still received light. Since they flew normally, blocked light, not paint, caused the problem. This is a control group.$q$),
