None of these efforts alone solves the problem. But together they reflect a broader understanding: access to healthy food depends not only on where a store is but on whether people can realistically use it.$q$, $q$According to the passage, in rural areas the distance used to identify a food desert is often:$q$, $q$["twenty miles", "five miles", "ten miles", "one mile"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Paragraph 1: "in rural areas, the distance used is often ten miles."$q$),
