Such audits require one thing above all: a paper record of each vote. A purely electronic system leaves nothing independent to check the machines against. For this reason, many election experts recommend that every voting system produce a paper ballot that the voter can see before it is cast.$q$, $q$According to the passage, in a risk-limiting audit, a closer race generally requires:$q$, $q$["checking more ballots", "checking fewer ballots", "only a machine recount", "no audit at all"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$"In a close race, many more ballots must be checked."$q$),
